<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
      Ethiopian monthly PAYE bands are CONFIGURATION DATA seeded PER COMPANY
      from the reference calculator's PAYE_BAND_GENERATIONS (the single source
      of truth the fast goldens test). BOTH generations are seeded:
      Proclamation 979/2016, and Income Tax (Amendment) Proclamation 1395/2025
      (tax-free <= 2,000; top 35% above 14,000) in force from 8 July 2025 —
      the 2025 reform, not "2024/25" as this comment previously said, and the
      reason a payslip dated before that boundary must not use these bands.
      This runs on install AND every upgrade, so every company —
      not just the one active at install (A1) — owns real, effective-dated band
      records. Existing rows are never touched, so a client's tuned bands and
      historical generations are preserved. VERIFY against the Ministry of
      Revenue before payroll go-live; a future proclamation is a NEW generation
      of records, never an edit to these.
    -->
    <function model="l10n.et.paye.band" name="_l10n_et_seed_all_companies"/>
</odoo>
